# The ledger of `http2`: HTTP/2 (RFC 9113) and HPACK (RFC 7541), against
# Go 1.27's golang.org/x/net/http2 v0.63.0 (with http2/hpack and http2/h2c),
# Rust's h2 0.4 (docs built 2026-11-18) and Python 3.15's h2 4.4.1, hpack
# 4.2.0 and hyperframe 6.1.0, listed from this machine on 2026-11-18.

capability frame/read  a frame read from bytes or a stream, every check of RFC 9113 § 4 and § 6 made
  heroes  http2.decode_frame, http2.read_frame
  go      net/http2.ErrFrameTooLarge, net/http2.Flags, net/http2.Flags.Has, net/http2.Frame, net/http2.FrameHeader, net/http2.FrameHeader.Header, net/http2.FrameHeader.String, net/http2.FrameWriteRequest.StreamID, net/http2.Framer, net/http2.Framer.ErrorDetail, net/http2.Framer.ReadFrame, net/http2.Framer.ReadFrameForHeader, net/http2.Framer.ReadFrameHeader, net/http2.Framer.SetMaxReadFrameSize, net/http2.Length, net/http2.NewFramer, net/http2.ReadFrameHeader, net/http2.StreamID, net/http2.Type
  rust    -
  python  hyperframe.frame.FRAMES, hyperframe.frame.FRAME_MAX_ALLOWED_LEN, hyperframe.frame.FRAME_MAX_LEN, hyperframe.frame.Flag, hyperframe.frame.Flags, hyperframe.frame.Frame, hyperframe.frame.Frame.explain, hyperframe.frame.Frame.parse_body, hyperframe.frame.Frame.parse_flags, hyperframe.frame.Frame.parse_frame_header
  note    a payload past the largest frame is refused from its head, before its bytes are read; a PRIORITY frame not of 5 bytes ends its stream alone as RFC 9113 § 6.3 says, where Go ends the connection (observed 2026-11-18 with x/net v0.63.0)

capability frame/write  a frame written, each field held to its range
  heroes  http2.encode_frame, http2.write_frame
  go      net/http2.AllowIllegalReads, net/http2.AllowIllegalWrites, net/http2.Framer.WriteContinuation, net/http2.Framer.WriteData, net/http2.Framer.WriteDataPadded, net/http2.Framer.WriteGoAway, net/http2.Framer.WriteHeaders, net/http2.Framer.WritePing, net/http2.Framer.WritePriority, net/http2.Framer.WritePriorityUpdate, net/http2.Framer.WritePushPromise, net/http2.Framer.WriteRSTStream, net/http2.Framer.WriteRawFrame, net/http2.Framer.WriteSettings, net/http2.Framer.WriteSettingsAck, net/http2.Framer.WriteWindowUpdate
  rust    -
  python  hyperframe.frame.Frame.serialize, hyperframe.frame.Frame.serialize_body
  note    bytes observed equal to Go 1.27 x/net v0.63.0 Framer's for every type, padding and priority included; a field out of range fails invalid where Go writes it under AllowIllegalWrites

